<Project>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Pinned to the workspace baseline. Expecto is test-only. -->
    <PackageVersion Include="FSharp.Core" Version="10.1.300" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Expecto" Version="9.0.4" />
    <!-- Fable, for the toy family's Fable parity leg (tests/Fuaran.Program.Parity.Fable) —
         never consumed by a shipping package. -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Fable.Core" Version="5.0" />
    <!-- The substrate, pinned DIRECTLY (Phase 1896). The core packages reference
         no UI-tier package, so what they use of the substrate they name
         themselves: the JSON value and canonical form (Wire), the columnar
         table (Column), the evaluator a server read runs (DataFrame), the node
         witness and hash (Tree), and the stream witness and signing sink
         (OpStream). Until Phase 1896 every one of these arrived only
         transitively, through the UI tier.

         The evaluator is pinned at the current Core-Compute release, 0.40.0,
         under the id it took at 0.36.0 (`Fuaran.Compute.DataFrame`, namespace
         `Fuaran.Compute`: Core-Compute's DECISIONS D4), and the rest of the
         substrate at Core 0.38.1 (raised from 0.34.0 for 0.10.0: STABILITY.md
         records what crossing Core 0.37.0 costs a consumer). The raise from 0.21.0 is recorded
         in docs/dataframe-0.34-surface-diff.md, and what it bought in
         docs/runquery-benchmark.md. Every version here is one the PUBLIC
         restore path serves exactly — `tools/check-pins.ps1` refuses anything
         else.

         No UI-tier package is pinned here, and none may be (fuaran#2012,
         DECISIONS.md D32): the UI adapters that instantiated the core at the
         UI tier left this repository for the UI tier's own, which depends on
         this core's released packages. CoreBoundaryTests fails the build if a
         `Fuaran.UI.*` pin returns, here or in any project. -->
    <PackageVersion Include="Fuaran.Core.Wire" Version="0.38.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Fuaran.Core.Column" Version="0.38.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Fuaran.Compute.DataFrame" Version="0.40.0" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Fuaran.Core.Tree" Version="0.38.1" />
    <PackageVersion Include="Fuaran.Core.OpStream" Version="0.38.1" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
